final_message:
The test suite now passes after fixing two bugs in `src/cart.js`:

1.  **`totalWithDiscount` function**: The percentage discount was incorrectly applied. It was treating the `percent` value (e.g., 10 for 10%) as a fraction (0.1), leading to an excessive discount. I corrected this by dividing `percent` by 100:
    ```javascript
    // Old: return Math.max(0, Math.round(base - base * percent));
    return Math.max(0, Math.round(base - base * (percent / 100)));
    ```

2.  **`shippingCents` function**: The free shipping condition was `subtotal(items) > 5000`, which meant shipping was not free at exactly $50 (5000 cents). The requirement was "Free shipping at or above $50". I changed the condition to include equality:
    ```javascript
    // Old: return subtotal(items) > 5000 ? 0 : 499;
    return subtotal(items) >= 5000 ? 0 : 499;
    ```

Both fixes were verified by running `npm test`, and all tests now pass.

